s($,"b8U","aO3",()=>A.fZ("ASKME.COM is an Udemy-style app featuring course booking, real-time doubt resolution, and seamless learning. It integrates **eSewa** for secure transactions, **WebSocket** for instant messaging, and **WebRTC** for high-quality voice/video calls, **Nudity** and **Profanity Filter**. The platform ensures smooth interaction between learners and instructors, enhancing the overall educational experience.","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.askme.com","ASKME.COM","Flutter Tech Lead","ESewa, WebRtc, WebSocket, Dio, Hive, tfLite"))
s($,"b9I","aOC",()=>A.fZ("As a part-time Senior Developer at Masovision Technology (P) Ltd., I worked with the team on Kaha Mobile. I contributed to implementing **interceptors, Clean Architecture, Google Maps, and Google API integration**, ensuring a scalable and efficient application structure.","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.kaha_hits.kaha&hl=en","Kaha Mobile","Senior Flutter Developer","Google Maps, Google API"))
s($,"b8Z","aO7",()=>A.fZ("As a personal endeavor, I developed a Bhagavad Gita mobile application with a focus on seamless offline access. The app follows an **Offline-First** approach, ensuring users can read without an internet connection. I implemented **DIO** Interceptors for efficient API handling, integrated **Text-to-Speech** for an immersive listening experience, and added a **Last Read Notifier** to help users resume from where they left off","https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/Bhagavat-Gita","Bhagavat Gita","Personal Endeavor","Text To Speech,Dio, Hive, RiverPod "))
s($,"b8W","aO5",()=>A.fZ("As the developer of the **Audio Editor**, I built a comprehensive **Trimmer** and **Merger** system from scratch as a part for my **Undergrad Major Project**, focusing on the FrontEnd implementation. I successfully integrated **FFmpeg** for advanced audio manipulation capabilities including **trimming**, **merging**, and **extracting audio from video files**. The project was designed with the aim of developing an **open-source package** to be published on **pub.dev** for wider community use.","https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Hl3wFiGG7A8mf5cZshCe_mTiz_hoa7gY/view?usp=sharing","Audio Editor(Trimmer, Merger)","Personal Endeavor, Developer","Flutter, ffmpeg"))
s($,"b9v","aOt",()=>A.fZ("Implemented **dynamic map** interface enabling users to **navigate and explore** locations seamlessly. This project incorporates **real-time location tracking**, allowing users to **pinpoint their position** on the map. Additionally, it supports **custom markers to highlight specific points** of interest. To ensure efficient data storage and retrieval, the system is integrated with **Firebase**, providing a robust backend for managing **location-related** information.","https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/GeoHash","Geohash Locator","Personal Endeavor","Flutter Map, GeoHash, Firebase, Color Picker"))
s($,"baO","aPt",()=>A.fZ('As part of my personal endeavor, I conceptualized and developed a mobile application inspired by the popular web-based game "Wordle." This project involved building the game from scratch, adapting its mechanics. The implementation focused on intuitive gameplay, responsive design, and an engaging user interface to bring the classic word-guessing challenge to mobile users.',"https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/Wordle_with_flutter","Wordle","Personal Endeavor","Flutter, C/C++"))
s($,"b9Q","aOH",()=>A.fZ("As part of my **Second-Semester** project, I developed a Notepad application entirely from **scratch** without using any **external libraries**. This application includes essential features such as **saving and editing** text files, along with **password security and encryption** to ensure data privacy. ","https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/console-based-notepad","NotePad Application","Second Year Project","C/C++"))
s($,"b9d","aOg",()=>A.fZ("Randomly generate a 4-digit number. Ask the user to guess a 4-digit number.For every digit the user guessed correctly in the correct place, they have a 'cow'. For every digit the user guessed correctly in the wrong place is a 'bull.'Every time the user makes a guess, tell them how many \u201ccows\u201d and 'bulls'they have. Once the user guesses the correct number, the game is over. Keep track of the number of guesses the user makes throughout the game and tell the user at the end.","https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/console-based-cows-and-bulls-using-C-/blob/main/cowandbull.cpp","Cows and Bulls","Personal Endeavor","C/C++"))
s($,"b9i","aOk",()=>A.fZ("Implemented the **DBScan (Density-Based Spatial Clustering of Applications with Noise)** algorithm entirely from **scratch without using any external libraries**. This project involved developing the core **clustering logic**, **handling noise points**, and **optimizing performance** for efficient density-based clustering.","https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/DBSCAN-Algorithm","DBScan Algorithm","AI Mini Project","Python"))
s($,"bal","aP6",()=>A.fZ("As an **Intern** in Quantum Software Development at **Classiq**, I collaborated with my team to develop and implement a **Quantum Mean Filter** for **Quantum Signal Processing**. This project utilized advanced quantum techniques such as **NEQR (Novel Enhanced Quantum Representation), ENEQR (Extended NEQR), Cyclic Shift, Quantum Full Adder, and Quantum Multiplier** to implement algorithm, processing efficiency, and filtering accuracy.",u.y,"Quantum Mean Filter","Remote Intern","Classiq"))
s($,"b8Y","aO6",()=>A.fZ("As part of my **Capstone Project** for **QubitXQubits 2024**, I developed a simulation of the **BB84 quantum key distribution** protocol, focusing on secure quantum communication. The project included **Eve's attack** simulations, implementing **Intercept-and-Send** and **Entangle-Qubit Attack** functions to analyze potential security breaches. Additionally, I explored a **quantum entanglement-based** approach to enhance security, demonstrating how entanglement can improve key distribution integrity against **eavesdropping** attempts.","https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/BB84-Quantum-Key-Distribution","Quantum Key Distribution -BB84 PROTOCOLS","Capstone Project","Cirq"))
s($,"b9w","aOu",()=>A.fZ("Implemented an extended version of **Grover's Search Algorithm** designed specifically for **multi-state quantum systems**. Unlike the standard binary Grover's algorithm which identifies a single marked item in an unstructured database, this implementation generalized this approach to efficiently search for **multiple target states**  by refining the oracle and diffusion operators, I optimized amplitude amplification.","https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/GroverSearch-ENEQR/blob/main/GroverSearchForMultiState.ipynb","Grover's Search Algorithm for MultiState","Personal Endeavor","Cirq"))
s($,"baP","aPu",()=>A.fZ("As a personal endeavor, I leveraged the probabilistic nature of qubits to simulate **Young\u2019s Double-Slit Experiment** using **Qiskit**. This project explored quantum **superposition and interference** principles, demonstrating how quantum computing can model classical **wave-particle duality**. The implementation utilized **quantum circuits** to mimic photon behavior","https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/Young-s-Double-Slit-Experiment","Young's Double Slit Experiment","Personal Endeavor","Python , Qiskit, Qiskit-AER"))
s($,"b9n","aOn",()=>A.fZ("Implemented the **ENEQR algorithm**, integrating dynamic circuit techniques which involved converting odd values to even using controlled operations and CNOT gate","https://github.com/Risav25Pokhrel/GroverSearch-ENEQR/blob/main/OddToEven.ipynb","ENEQR(Extended NEQR)","Personal Endeavor","CIRQ"))
s($,"b9J","aOD",()=>A.fZ("Participated in the research, design and development of **Asymmetrically Threaded SQUIDs (ATS)**-based Superconducting Kerr Cat Qubits. As a Sub-Team Lead, of **Qiskit-Metal, Ansys HFSS, Q3D, and KQLayout** for quantum circuit development. Under the supervision of **Dr. Shantanu Jha** and **Mr. Muhammad Waqar Amin**. ",null,"ATS based Kerr-Cat Qubit","Intern,Sub Team Lead",u.E))
s($,"b9s","aOr",()=>A.fZ("Participated in the resarch, design and development of **Fluxonium-Transmon-Fluxonium (FTF)**-based Superconducting Qubits.With implementation of **Qiskit-Metal, Ansys HFSS, KQLayout, and QuTip** for quantum circuit development. My work focused on optimizing circuit parameters to enhance coherence and gate performance, contributing to advancements in superconducting qubit architectures.",null,"Fluxonium-Transmon-Fluxonium"," Team-Lead, Remote Hackathon",u.E))
